WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.160
The comment section on this one is gonna be
hell.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.920
Do your worst, you filthy animals.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.460
Now, before we begin today’s video, let’s
clear some things up.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.180
We know exactly what you’re thinking.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.789
“An Among Us SCP?

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:21.250
This sounds ridiculous!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.230
Why would the Foundation ever have to deal
with an anomaly relating to Among Us, of all

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.230
things?

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.189
Is this some sick joke dreamt up by our YouTube
commenters?”

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:32.070
And we get it.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.260
It’s definitely one of the more ridiculous
anomalies the Foundation has had to contain,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.550
at least at face value.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.390
But there are a few things you should take
into consideration before things get too Amogus-pilled

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.020
around here.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.899
First, this is hardly the strangest anomaly
we’ve covered on SCP Explained!

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:57.351
SCP-5981, also known as Nuke City, revolved
around a mysterious broadcast of a Family

00:00:57.351 --> 00:00:58.980
Guy episode!

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.640
SCP-4335, a Welt in the Crucible, had to deal
with an entity occupying space inside the

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.730
video game Minecraft.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.740
But there are countless other examples of
anomalies creeping into popular culture, mutating

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.940
it, and twisting it for their own purposes.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.530
What may seem silly on paper, such as the
Foundation having to do research on a popular

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.560
video game like Among Us, is all part of what
the organization does.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.110
If the brave researchers at the SCP Foundation
chuckled and brushed off a potential threat

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:34.350
just because it had to do with something like
Among Us, the entire population might be susceptible

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.160
to a supernatural event of unprecedented proportions.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.659
The Foundation’s entire Veil of secrecy
could crumble, all because someone shrugged

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:47.250
off the possibility of allocating resources
to deal with a threat millions of civilians

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.710
could discover.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:54.909
These games, movies, and shows are immensely
popular, and an anomaly affecting a global

00:01:54.909 --> 00:02:00.399
phenomenon like Among Us could spell doom
for not only the Foundation, but the entire

00:02:00.399 --> 00:02:02.960
world as well, if left unchecked.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.680
So, if you don’t want to risk termination,
please try to keep a straight face as we divulge

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:16.610
into the weird and wacky story of SCP-5167,
an anomaly codenamed in the Foundation’s

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:22.150
database as “When the Impostor is Sus”.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:25.640
I hate my job sometimes.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.020
To begin, we need to go back.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.200
Way, way back.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.410
Centuries before Among Us was even conceived
as a concept, before video games had been

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:39.610
invented, and even before electricity itself
was discovered.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:45.610
Back to an era where the gods of Olympus ruled
supreme, and stone, marble statues lined buildings

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:51.460
that would serve as timeless feats of architecture,
and where a new school of thought was developing.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.090
One that focused on logic and reason instead
of superstition and hearsay.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.650
That’s right, we’re talking about ancient
Greece.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:03.870
A society that, for all of its achievements
and progression in the fields of education,

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.030
cultures, and logic, was still largely governed
by religion and mythology.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:13.610
But of course, as you may come to expect when
dealing with the SCP Foundation, there’s

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.450
always a little truth in that which we cannot
understand.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:22.550
While those who are unaware of the paranormal
might deride the Greeks for being overly focused

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:27.360
on a pantheon of gods they logically should
have had no reason to believe, those who know

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.350
that anything can happen in the world of the
anomalous may approach this topic, and the

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.590
subject of religion in general, in a different
light.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.420
The Greek gods were very real.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:43.390
While the myths may not be entirely true,
and they may not have been literal gods, there

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:49.350
were a group of anomalous entities who influenced
Greek society, performing miraculous feats

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:54.090
that left those who observed them in complete
wonder and putting together cults of worship

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.520
surrounding them.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.470
While most of this was done in secret, word
of these beings traveled incredibly fast in

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.470
the ancient world, and they were heralded
as gods.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:09.730
Beings of divine might that could do anything
in the universe, who existed above the mortal

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.990
plane, and demanded worship from their followers.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:18.180
A glance at Greek mythology paints a picture
of a group of gods who acted, more or less,

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.180
like humans.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.480
They fought, they killed, they argued, and
they felt human emotions.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.880
It’s likely that this characterization in
the stories emerged from how these entities

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:30.370
conducted themselves in actuality.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.920
There were dozens upon dozens of entities
the Greeks worshiped as divinity, and while

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:39.550
the stories portrayed the gods as jealous,
vengeful beings, who constantly fought with

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:45.840
each other, it doesn’t compare to the reality
of the situation, which was much more cut-throat.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.680
You see, there were the twelve gods of Olympus,
and you probably know most of them.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.630
They’re remembered today for a reason.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:57.630
Zeus, Athena, Poseidon, Ares, the list goes
on.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:02.850
We still remember these beings because of
the iconic stories they took part in, and

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:05.850
how significant they were in ancient times.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:10.580
Well, for every Zeus, God of Lightning, there
were five more gods who absolutely no one

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.350
but the most hardcore historical fanatic remember.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:20.130
Gods of niche subjects, who had small followings,
who never had those character-defining myths

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.510
to flesh them out and preserve them for all
of history to remember.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.950
Who would, when Greece fell, fade into obscurity.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.310
For every Zeus, there was a Phthonus.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.990
Who was Phthonus, you ask?

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.180
Well, if the guy heard you asking that question,
he’d probably smite you down before the

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.180
question even left your lips…

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:43.240
If he wasn’t engaged in a hardcore game
of Among Us, that is.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.460
Don’t worry, we’ll get there.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:47.050
All will be explained.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.270
It’s in the name of the channel, after all.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:55.150
Phthonus was a god of jealousy and envy, mainly
in a romantic context.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.480
Do you have a crush on someone who's already
taken?

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.920
Phthonus knows all about that.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.620
Do you wish you weren’t trapped in a dead-end
relationship with someone who doesn’t love

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:05.620
you?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.180
Phthonus understands your plight.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.410
But Phthonus wasn’t just a reverse, bizarro
Cupid.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:17.090
He was a literal personification of the emotions
of jealousy and envy themselves.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:22.390
No matter the context, if it was petty and
greedy, Phthonus knew it all too well.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:27.360
You would think this would make Phthonus a
prime candidate for some mythological drama,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.360
right?

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.800
After all, the Greek gods loved their in-fighting,
and who better to stir up some “Hera said,

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.650
Zeus said” arguments than a literal god
of envy?

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:39.680
Well, it didn’t quite work out that way
for Phthonus.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.680
His appearances in myths were infrequent,
and today, he is nearly all but forgotten.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:50.150
Reduced to a mere three sentences on a Wikipedia
page, while other figures from his era have

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:57.280
taken on an entire new life in the modern
day, as cultural icons like Perseus or Hercules.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:03.100
But not poor Phthonus, whose penchant for
jealousy and envy backfired on him, and catapulted

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.260
him into obscurity.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:06.340
Why did this happen?

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.010
It’s kind of obvious, when you think about
it.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:13.140
While other gods granted their worshippers
a good harvest, or copious amounts of wine

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:19.190
and partying, all that Phthonus had to offer
was, well, the ugly side of humanity.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.950
His worshippers were far and few between.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:26.169
After all, no one wanted their entire life
to revolve around the jealousy of others,

00:07:26.169 --> 00:07:30.740
and Phthonus, being a personification of envy,
had an understandably difficult time getting

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:33.250
people to devote themselves to him.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.720
Phthonus was greedy and envied the other gods.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.669
So while he would accept nothing but absolute
worship from his followers, he couldn’t

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:47.150
offer much else, especially not when compared
to the bountiful boons a great god like Zeus

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.530
or Hera could offer.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.950
And so, Phthonus festered.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:56.180
An ugly god, who wallowed in self-hatred and
irrelevancy, constantly living in the shadow

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.680
of the pantheon that gave him purpose.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:02.060
And his purpose was to remain jealous.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:06.740
To remain envious of those who had what he
did not.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:12.470
A god unfit to be worshiped, whose purpose
was to embody the feelings of wanting what

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.080
isn’t yours.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:20.040
Phthonus is both tragic, and poetic, and when
the Greeks faded away, so too did Phthonus.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:25.020
The Roman Empire, who largely adapted Greece’s
pantheon of gods for their own stories, left

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.910
no record of bringing Phthonus into the mix.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:33.190
For centuries, he was a god without a home,
attempting to find a place in a changing world.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:37.810
Phthonus was angry, jealous, envious, and
tired.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:42.490
The forces of the universe would call him
forth in every new era, thrusting him back

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:47.160
into the world and forcing him to search for
the sustenance beings that were referred to

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.090
as gods fed off of - devotion.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:54.450
But every time Phthonus would find himself
walking the earth once again, he would instead

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:58.240
discover that there was no place for him.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.570
Mankind was moving on.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:03.290
There was less and less room for gods with
every passing year.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:08.380
All the popular ones had established themselves
as everlasting religious figures at this point,

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.380
and they would never fade away.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:15.350
Some took pleasure in living among humans,
rising to power as people of influence and

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.350
fame.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:20.560
Others, who could not find a place in the
world, would fade away, never to be revived

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.370
or worshiped ever again.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.750
Forgotten, dead gods, who the world long outgrew.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:30.750
But Phthonus’ jealous spirit would never
allow him to consign himself to that fate.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:37.570
He hated who he was and what he stood for,
but that nature brought him back so many times

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.580
before.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:43.160
It was his jealousy of the other gods, who
were somehow managing to linger beyond their

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.020
Greek heyday, that caused him to persevere.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.340
He needed a purpose.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.290
One last chance to be remembered.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:56.660
He had struggled for centuries, and this was
his last-ditch effort to be remembered.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:02.220
Wherever he would wake up, in the modern era,
Phthonus would have to make the most of it.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:05.410
And this is where Among Us comes in.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:10.440
In late 2020, The SCP Foundation was just
as captivated as anyone else by the Among

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.500
Us phenomenon.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:16.010
A game that was sweeping the globe, where
players took on the roles of crewmates on

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:21.540
a spaceship, one of which was an impostor,
whose job was to secretly murder the other

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.540
players.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:26.371
While they were busy doing tasks that ranged
from scanning themselves in the medbay, or

00:10:26.371 --> 00:10:32.190
scanning keycards in the admin room, the impostor
would be lurking behind every corner, sometimes

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:36.250
in the ship’s air-vents, waiting for the
proper moment to strike.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:40.560
If a dead body was found, a player could report
it, and the players would then discuss which

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.610
one of them they suspected to be the impostor.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:48.430
The game’s addictive psychological elements
and accessible rules made it a smash hit,

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:53.060
but for the Foundation, they were infatuated
with it for entirely different reasons.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:58.460
You see, when a piece of media attains the
level of fame that Among Us did, the Foundation

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:01.020
has to make sure to keep their eyes on it.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.020
Popular media is a prime target for anomalies.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:07.440
The population’s collective attention on
it just seems to invite the forces of the

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:12.010
supernatural world to warp and distort what
we know to be familiar.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:16.050
And this is exactly what was happening to
Among Us.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:20.490
For months, the Foundation was documenting
cases of an entity who appeared in games of

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:23.920
Among Us and caused havoc in the real world.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:29.320
These cases, and their after-effects, were
so severe that the Foundation deemed the anomaly

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:34.430
significant enough to get its own file in
the database, designating it under the name

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:36.800
SCP-5167.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:42.040
SCP-5167 would join games of Among Us like
any other player.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.640
They would blend in, much like the impostor
in the game, and play just as anyone else

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.640
would.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:54.459
It was what happened after a player participated
in a session with SCP-5167 that had the Foundation

00:11:54.459 --> 00:11:57.640
investigating every aspect of the game.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:03.930
Those who played with SCP-5167 would find
themselves stricken by a severe case of paranoia

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:09.220
and Capgras delusion, a psychological condition
in which a victim would come to believe those

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:13.230
around them had been replaced with identical
impostors.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:18.110
The severity of this disorder varied between
individuals, but some believed the delusions

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:23.740
to such an extent that they lashed out at
those they believed to be impostors, sometimes

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.840
resulting in a homicide.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:31.020
Naturally, the Foundation put two and two
together, which led back to Among Us.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:35.000
After several months of police cases relating
to completely average individuals suddenly

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:39.900
striking out at their loved ones, sometimes
killing them, and showing signs of Capgras

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.990
delusion, the organization knew that something
was happening on an anomalous scale.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.420
At first, it was difficult to make the connection
to Among Us, but the Foundation eventually

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:54.050
learned, from interviews with victims and
an examination of their habits over the past

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.060
few weeks, that they had all played the game.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.510
And through analysis of the Among Us community’s
various trends and habits, the Foundation

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:08.649
discovered SCP-5167, an entity that was slowly
gaining notoriety within the game’s community

00:13:08.649 --> 00:13:11.600
as an almost mythological figure.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:16.730
SCP-5167’s tendency to spout long, wordy
rants at other players during the game’s

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:21.950
emergency meeting sessions positioned them
as an inside joke for those who encountered

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:22.950
them.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:27.070
Needing to establish a link between these
anomalously induced bouts of paranoia, the

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:34.209
Foundation set up a group of web-crawler AIs
to track Among Us game sessions until SCP-5167

00:13:34.209 --> 00:13:35.220
would appear.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:39.779
It was a long shot, but it was one of many
different theories on why these victims were

00:13:39.779 --> 00:13:45.180
undergoing this level of psychosis, and if
it proved to be true, then the Foundation

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:48.560
would have a solid idea of what to do next.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:54.339
After weeks of nothing, SCP-5167 was spotted
in a game, and the Foundation acted quickly

00:13:54.339 --> 00:13:58.110
to track down the other players who played
alongside the entity.

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:03.520
Naturally, they exhibited signs of paranoia
and delusion, some of them only for weeks,

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.240
and others for months.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:09.560
That was enough evidence for the Foundation,
who would later document several other occurrences

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:16.130
of games with SCP-5167 resulting in these
psychiatric conditions in other players.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:20.440
The Foundation did what they do best, and
established a series of Special Containment

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:26.390
Procedures that would wipe SCP-5167 from the
internet as best as they could.

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:30.390
Web crawlers were trained to take down any
mentions of the entity, and if a potential

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.899
sighting was discovered, the Foundation would
investigate any and all players involved in

00:14:34.899 --> 00:14:36.080
the incident.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:41.649
Anyone affected by SCP-5167 would be held
under the guise of receiving medical treatment

00:14:41.649 --> 00:14:46.110
for mental health issues, and they would be
amnesticized completely.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:51.560
You might be thinking that the aftereffects
of SCP-5167 are relatively tame compared to

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:55.080
what the Foundation usually deals with, but
look at it this way.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.490
Among Us is a game played by millions of people.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:05.180
If SCP-5167 affected only a fraction of that
population, it would spell total chaos for

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.420
the Foundation.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.339
Not only that, but the amount of bloodshed
the entity could cause would be nothing to

00:15:10.339 --> 00:15:15.089
scoff at, as a large amount of cases dealt
with victims outright murdering anyone they

00:15:15.089 --> 00:15:17.970
suspected to be an impostor.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:23.060
Attempts to track down the SCP-5167 entity
were met with failure.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.990
All points of internet access that the Foundation
was able to get their hands on only led to

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:30.760
a series of abandoned home addresses in rural
Greece.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:33.970
But over time, things started to change.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:37.440
The Foundation began to place less of a concern
on SCP-5167.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:41.450
It was almost as if the entity was being forgotten.

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.450
Why?

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:47.760
This letter, addressed to the SCP-5167 research
team from the Site’s director, might clear

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:48.990
some things up.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:54.600
As requested by Head Researcher Abrams, I've
had the Site-22 analysts look into the progress

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:00.390
of SCP-5167's anomalous effects over the period
we've observed it — and the results are

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.029
much as I expected.

00:16:02.029 --> 00:16:07.820
When we first discovered SCP-5167 — for
the sake of argument, let's say this is when

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:13.890
SCP-5167 first came into existence — the
impact it had on its victims was severe.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:18.800
I don't think I have to remind you of what
Billy Heth did to his family's faces.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:23.070
But since then — almost immediately, really,
since that first couple of manifestations

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:26.110
— the potency of its effects has started
to decline.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:31.839
Full detachment from reality became delusion,
and delusion has now become paranoia - and

00:16:31.839 --> 00:16:35.660
the intensity of that paranoia is lessening
in each new case.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:40.240
This is all conjecture, of course, and shouldn't
be taken as gospel — but based on what we've

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:47.690
observed of this anomaly thus far, our estimation
is that SCP-5167's anomalous effects will

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.959
become inert by the end of the year.

00:16:49.959 --> 00:16:54.880
Whether it'll keep popping up in these video
game matches is another story, though.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:58.500
It was just as the director had explained.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.779
SCP-5167’s cases were becoming less severe.

00:17:01.779 --> 00:17:07.350
They were almost becoming irrelevant, so much
so that the Foundation hypothesized that the

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:11.389
anomaly’s declining potency would lead to
its neutralization before long.

00:17:11.389 --> 00:17:15.439
An entity fading into irrelevance and obscurity
once more.

00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:20.730
If you haven’t figured it out yet, maybe
SCP-5167’s username will spell it out for

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:21.730
you.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:26.459
When the entity joined games of Among Us,
it made sure that everyone knew who it was.

00:17:26.459 --> 00:17:31.090
Well, everyone would know who it was if the
entity had managed to maintain any form of

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.950
popularity over the past dozen centuries or
so.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.789
That’s right.

00:17:36.789 --> 00:17:40.370
SCP-5167 would join under the name Phthonus.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:45.610
The god’s new life had thrust it into the
modern-day, except this time it was inside

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:50.130
the game of Among Us, where it was forced
to cope with the reality that the world seemed

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:55.419
to be more obsessed with a trendy game than
any god or mythological figure.

00:17:55.419 --> 00:17:59.269
While inside the game, Phthonus was one bitter
individual.

00:17:59.269 --> 00:18:03.779
During emergency meetings, instead of trying
to figure out if red was sus or not, the god

00:18:03.779 --> 00:18:05.970
would just yell at the players around him!

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:08.970
One player asked Phthonus what they were doing
while the rest of the crew was performing

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.109
their tasks.

00:18:10.109 --> 00:18:12.370
To which, Phthonus poetically responded.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:13.370
“Where was I?

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:17.460
I was there when the mountains were newborn,
and the oceans virginal.

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:23.039
I was there when gods walked among men, and
their wisdom was cast down like sunlight.

00:18:23.039 --> 00:18:26.700
I was there when mankind was capable of legends.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:27.879
And now?

00:18:27.879 --> 00:18:33.179
I find myself in a world that has forgotten
even the taste of life, even the very concept

00:18:33.179 --> 00:18:36.389
of life beyond existing from one day to the
next.

00:18:36.389 --> 00:18:37.460
Mere continuance.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:42.580
Where all the world is wasted away in idle
play of emotions that once rang true.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:50.230
I am in a world where even the gods are forgotten,
their bones washed away by time.

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:54.379
A world where man has moved on, where all
the legacy I have left are three sentences

00:18:54.379 --> 00:18:55.970
on Wikipedia.

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:58.230
I thought my time had come again.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:00.220
I thought this could be the new me.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.029
But this is nothing.

00:19:02.029 --> 00:19:04.149
Let me stay dead this time.

00:19:04.149 --> 00:19:05.909
I'm tired.”

00:19:05.909 --> 00:19:10.149
To which, the other players responded, in
typical Among Us fashion, that Phthonus was

00:19:10.149 --> 00:19:11.230
“sus”.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:15.220
He was promptly voted as the impostor, and
ejected from the airlock.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:18.840
And so, the tragic tale of Phthonus came to
a close.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.999
A tired, obscure God who never had a place
in the world.

00:19:22.999 --> 00:19:27.499
His presence in Among Us grew less and less
as the game’s popularity waned, and once

00:19:27.499 --> 00:19:30.039
again he would fade into obscurity.

00:19:30.039 --> 00:19:35.600
But the nature of Phthonus meant that he would,
in some form, return one day.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.690
Where, or how, no one could say.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:44.639
But as long as there was a situation to reap
envy from, a trend to be jealous of, Phthonus

00:19:44.639 --> 00:19:49.559
would remain, eternally doomed to suffer the
fate of being nobody’s favorite god.

00:19:49.559 --> 00:19:53.409
And frankly, we can’t imagine this video
will change that.

00:19:53.409 --> 00:20:01.229
Now go check out “SCP Minecraft World Destroyer
SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible” and “SCP-5254

00:20:01.229 --> 00:20:04.879
- Gotta Catch 'Em All” for more of the most
absurd anomalies out there!

